# `_bmad-output` is ignored for NOISE, not for distribution (user, 2026-09-09) —
# `stories/` alone is 620K of per-story churn and the ledgers are working files.
#
# THE SIX DESIGN DOCUMENTS THE CODE CITES BY NAME ARE THE EXCEPTION. Dozens of
# comments across `core/` and `adapters/` cite them as the authority for a
# decision — `cost-model.md` 29 times, `pipeline-stages.md` 27,
# `host-integration.md` 16, `SPEC.md` 13 — and while the whole tree was ignored,
# not one of those citations resolved in a fresh clone. A comment pointing at a
# file nobody can open is worse than no comment: it reads as though the reasoning
# is written down somewhere.
#
# RE-INCLUDED ONE FILE AT A TIME, down a re-excluded path. git cannot descend
# into an excluded directory, so each level is opened (`!dir/`) and then its
# contents closed again (`dir/*`) before the next level opens. Un-ignoring
# `/_bmad-output/` alone exposes the whole tree — 41 files, ledgers and review
# dumps included — which is what this shape exists to prevent.
#
# Grepped, not guessed: these are exactly the `.md` paths the code cites, minus
# `deferred-work.md`, the working ledger, which stays local as local history.
/_bmad-output/*
!/_bmad-output/specs/
/_bmad-output/specs/*
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/
/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/*
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/SPEC.md
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/cost-model.md
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/host-integration.md
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/pipeline-stages.md
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/deferred-v2.md
!/_bmad-output/specs/spec-mad-orchestrator/survey-grounding.md

